            <div class="step2-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Unique Contribution</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-1.png">
                <p>The Member Archetype is one of the three archetypes who desire nothing more but to connect with others and attain a sense of belonging.This is the Members&rsquo; unique contribution to the world, and also how The Member Archetype makes sense of the world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>To the Member, it&rsquo;s not possible to connect with others if you don&rsquo;t belong and vice versa.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Members do not yearn for intimacy like the Lover as a form of connection, nor do they seek connection through fun and enjoyment as the Jester does.Belonging is everything to the Member &ndash; the only way to do things.</p>
                <p>To attain a sense of belonging Member archetypes are incredibly sociable and find it easy to get along with everybody they encounter.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The Members&rsquo; secret weapon in helping them connect with others and establish a sense of belonging is their advanced listening and rapport building skills. Members are active listeners and can reflect that they have listened well to people they come into contact with which is an advanced but rare communication technique.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This communication tactic is also a great way to subliminally compliment and endorse the people who are communicating with The Member.It&rsquo;s important to note here, however, that the Member does not use this ability to control or manipulate situations, even though they probably could.This strategy usually comes naturally to the Member, and in all honesty, they might not even realize that this skill is so exceptional they just don&rsquo;t find it so easy to do things any other way.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>As you start to read on, you&rsquo;ll learn how, despite the Members ability to shine when it comes to networking and interacting with others, they also have some severe communication challenges too.Such difficulties can often jeopardize the Members ability to attain a sense of belonging or a deep sense of connection - this surprising problem is counter-intuitive to the Members goals and intentions.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Keep on reading on to reveal more about the challenges that The Member faces.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Different Levels of Connection</strong></p>
                <p>In many ways, the Members charisma and listening skills do indeed create a sense of belonging and connection but not necessarily for themselves though.The Member tends to be more successful at creating a sense of belonging through inspiring and assisting others to be able to connect and to feel as though they belong instead.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>They do this through their actions and ability to assist others in enhancing their social experiences and with their ability to connect precisely where and when it&rsquo;s needed.The Member uses these skills so that they might feel as though they belong too, but because of some of their greatest challenges, they often don&rsquo;t feel as connected as others might think.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Members support others socially very well because they can identify people and situations who have difficulties with connecting and belonging (socially) a mile away.This ability and attention to detail make the Member an excellent host or companion at social events.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The problem is, we don&rsquo;t achieve a deep sense of connection and belonging from our social interactions alone. Sure, we might achieve confirmation of our social prowess, but that&rsquo;s really about the limit.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>True Connection</strong></p>
                <p>If we don&rsquo;t learn how to feel part of something or connected deeply and personally without the need of social proof to endorse our sense of belonging, then we only receive a warped sense of connection. This warped sense of connection will be entirely dependent upon how others see us and how we perceive that others see us &mdash; a problem that can lead to superficial identities, low esteem, and confidence and a sense of lack.It could also lead to a sense of insecurity that pushes us further away from really feeling connected and as though we belong.</p>
                <p>The fallout from these experiences will be difficult for any archetype to handle, but they are more difficult for the Member to deal with, since they often unwittingly base their identity and sense of belonging on their social interactions.</p>
                <p>So, while the Member in part succeeds in their goals to create a sense of belonging and connection, they often do so for others rather than themselves.This means that to attain a sense of fulfillment for themselves they need to tweak their habits, behaviors, and perspective so that they can also feel the sense of connection and belonging they desire for themselves too.</p>
                <p>Keep on reading to find out how Members, experience such problems and also how they might overcome them in the future.</p>
