            <div class="step3-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Sense of Significance</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/sun-glow.png" style="filter:none">
                <p>Attaining a sense of significance is a vital need for everybody.If we don&rsquo;t figure out a way to feel significant, we can start to become stagnant, we might develop poor confidence, and our wellbeing begins to deplete.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Most people naturally figure out a way to develop their sense of significance, and in the case of The Member Archetype, they attain their significance feeling part of something.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Member archetypes are very likely to enjoy being part of a club, group or brotherhood.They&rsquo;d enjoy being part of a sports team, or part of a crafting circle - any group that involves the coming together of people is a fun place for a Member to be.A family group or group of friends are all examples of the types of groups that Members would be part of.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This is one of the ways in which a Member attains a sense of significance.</p>
                <p>There are some people in the world who don&rsquo;t enjoy being part of a club but the not the Member.They&rsquo;ll fully invest themselves in the experience and goals of whatever club or group they are involved in. If the Member is not part of a club or group and doesn&rsquo;t spend time socializing, they will start to feel alone and isolated from the world. This, in turn, will cause the Member to spiral downwards.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The Member needs social contact to attain a sense of significance and contribution above anything else.</p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step2-back hover f-left">2. Unique Contribution</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
                                <button class="btn step4 hover f-right">4. Personality Traits</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step4-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Personality Traits</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/floral.png">
                <p>The Member archetype has an uncanny ability for building rapport with people from all walks of life, and they can do so fast, without revealing too much about themselves in the process.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s this knack for rapport building that is admired by others and allows Members to build strong friendships built on trust, the Member loves this about themselves and wouldn&rsquo;t have it any other way.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Members live to interact with the world around them, but not in the way that the Explorer does where he or she has to experience different countries and cultures physically.Instead, the Member interacts by connecting with others.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This exceptional rapport building quality along with their ability to listen and hear what others say to them makes Members popular amongst the crowds. Members also often have balanced and sound morals and principles too, which are also admirable to others. It&rsquo;s easy to see why others connect with them so quickly.</p>
                <p><strong>Members Can Easily Get What They Want</strong></p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s easy for a Member to attain what he or she wants in general because their charisma and charm will see them through.And because of their advanced social qualities, Members often find it easy to be promoted in the workplace or to move through society as a result of networking.It also helps that others seem to want to tell the Member their deepest secrets, which in a sense, will appeal to the member&rsquo;s innate desires to feel a deep connection with others.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s this ability to connect with everyone that can cause challenges for the Member.Such challenges arise because Members' tend to attract a large crowd who may differ in morals and principles to the Member and may not always be so loyal or loving as the Member would hope.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>To be able to connect with so many, the Member has to hide themselves, they don&rsquo;t talk about themselves too much, and they prefer it this way.</p>
                <p>Members often hate the spotlight even though they are frequently thrown under it at any given moment due to their charisma and charm.They also don&rsquo;t like to reveal too much about themselves either for fear of rejection.Therefore, the perfect spot for a Member is mixed in amongst the crowd, not leading, directing, or speaking for the group.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Members build relationships quickly and often dislike feeling left out. However, because they don&rsquo;t take their time to get to know people well before establishing a strong connection and also because they don&rsquo;t show themselves to others, they often don&rsquo;t have as strong a bond with people as it would first seem. As such, even the Member is surprised when the friendship or relationship turns into a fleeting one.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The fast connections and fleeting relationships that the Member experiences often mean that it&rsquo;s easy for the Member to feel rejected, left out or disconnected in their interactions with others.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Members Can Be Disappointed in Their Relationships</strong></p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s not unusual for a Member to feel insulted and hurt when the attention on the friendship they&rsquo;ve created starts to die down.It&rsquo;s at this point the saying &lsquo;easy come, easy go&rsquo; springs to mind, and it certainly applies here in many of the Members fleeting friendships. It&rsquo;s just unfortunate that the Member takes these &lsquo;failed&rsquo; relationships so personally without stopping to ask why this might happen so frequently.</p>
                <p>Members can also experience challenges in relationships, yet they have no problem at all dating and connecting with others.However, when things become serious, they will feel as though their wings have been clipped if they cannot continue their social activities as they did before.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The social world is the lifeblood for a Member, and sometimes it clashes with their love life.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Members can also develop a seemingly deep connection quickly when it comes to romance because of their ability to listen and invest in people.But just like their friendships, they can find something to like and connect with, in most people, it&rsquo;s just that the same is not always reversed. This, once again, can leave the member feeling rejected and alone.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The Member needs to take their time to get to know people and to build on their relationships by making sure it&rsquo;s a two-way friendship where the Member contributes while they are connecting with the opportunity to see who they are.It would also help if they slowed down with the charm offensive so that they can see how invested the people around them are to them.</p>
                <p>In this way the Member can understand whether people are temporarily addicted to the Member's charm or interested in really getting to know them.The problem is that the Member will often take the lack of interest in them from a third party as being rejection rather than just everyday life.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Why Do We Hide Ourselves Even from Ourselves?</strong></p>
                <p>Every person has a hidden side.Jung calls it a shadow aspect, and it&rsquo;s discussed in great detail in our Premium Archetype Reports.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Here at Individuologist.com we realize that there is a hidden side or an unconscious world (to be more precise) that we experience internally, but we don&rsquo;t, or can't show or express this existence outwardly.It&rsquo;s this hidden aspect that can bring about great reward if we were to focus our attention on it. It&rsquo;s also crucial for helping each different archetype overcome their greatest challenge.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Before we get started, it&rsquo;s important to acknowledge that there&rsquo;s also a hidden part of us that remains unconscious even to ourselves too and the process of individuation can help us to uncover these hidden aspects of our &lsquo;self&rsquo; too.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>When we start to uncover these &lsquo;hidden&rsquo; aspects of our &lsquo;self,&rsquo; we begin to learn about what is really driving us.We discover the reasons why we do the things we do (or don&rsquo;t do the things that we want to do or should do).This gives us the opportunity to start to consciously reconcile these hidden aspects so that we can achieve our deepest desires or reach our fullest potential.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>In the case of The Member, their hidden personality traits often lie in understanding the reasons why they need to feel as though they belong, and why they find it difficult to attain a sense of belonging, even though they know how to interact very well socially.</p>
                <p>The Member archetype might seem to be socially adept to others, however internally, they don&rsquo;t like the spotlight to be on them (even though their social prowess usually brings such experiences to them!).They also don&rsquo;t feel relevant enough to want to show themselves to others.If you watch a Member in action, they&rsquo;ll make you feel entirely relevant and interesting, but they will often say little about themselves.</p>
                <p>As they self-identify based on how people perceive them and are afraid of rejection, the Member may unconsciously use their charm and charisma to avoid allowing people to see all of them.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This is a pattern that doesn&rsquo;t serve the Member very well because it poses the question; how can you feel as though you belong when you unconsciously hide all of yourself from somebody?There will be some part hidden deep inside the Members&rsquo; psyche that realizes that they don&rsquo;t belong, or that they only belong superficially because, to belong, we need to feel accepted fully, for our strengths and weaknesses.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This problem leads to a hidden low sense of esteem and an innate sense of, or fear of loneliness or of being alone.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>When the Member can recognize that they have some hidden patterns that are not serving them well, they realize that there are other ways to achieve their goals.When they realize that they have the opportunity to create a complete sense of connection and belonging, they can then let go of these hidden behavioral traits and truly experience a sense of connection, that is as deep as they dream of.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Members can achieve these goals through shadow work and other forms of individuation such as the Premium Archetype Report.</p>
                <p>Check out The Premium Archetype report to learn more about your Shadow Self and how to get started on the journey to individuation.</p>
