            <div class="step6-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Greatest Challenge</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/success.png">
                <p>Member archetypes focus on trying to find a way to belong. To attain a sense of connection and belonging and on the surface, they manage to achieve this very well.It&rsquo;s rare to find a Member who does not have a desirable social life, or who is not popular amongst their circle of friends or even amongst their family.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Sure, the Member will often be a vital member of whatever group or groups he or she is connected to, and they will seem to be surrounded by people who adore them, but for the Member, they feel far from adored.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>We&rsquo;ve already mentioned that the Member tends not to enjoy talking about themselves, usually because they fear rejection.They unconsciously often feel as though if they were to &lsquo;show&rsquo; themselves that they may not necessarily be as popular or accepted as they are when they don&rsquo;t show themselves.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This makes it difficult for a Member to feel as though they truly belong and yet the Member&rsquo;s primary concern is to feel as though they belong entirely.It makes sense and is probably very clear to others that all the Member needs to do to feel a deep sense of belonging is to allow others to see who they are, learn to accept themselves and understand that others will accept them too if they were to express themselves.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>But this is the Member&rsquo;s greatest challenge.</p>
                <p>The Member has an innate fear of rejection, and it is often unbearable for them to show themselves because the risk of rejection will way too high for them, and they will feel too vulnerable or exposed.So, they avoid it at all costs.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This pattern will always mean that if the Member doesn&rsquo;t make a conscious effort to change then the Member will never achieve the deep sense of connection and belonging that they live for because how can anybody build a relationship that connects deeply with somebody when they don&rsquo;t show who they are?The person that the Member is trying to relate to will have nothing to build on, and so the relationship becomes superficial.</p>
                <p>This means that the Member eventually creates a self-fulfilling prophecy where they will ultimately be rejected because they did not open up to the people close to them or it leads them to only experiencing superficial relationships which are far from what the Member wants.</p>
                <p>Unless the Member can learn to show themselves to others and learn to accept themselves, they will never achieve the connection and sense of belonging that they live for.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If the Member was willing to learn how to overcome their greatest challenge, then the story will be totally different.It will give the Member the opportunity to build relationships and connections in a way that they only dreamt of before.It will also help the Member to develop an innate sense of acceptance and belonging that they will carry in a strong sense of self for the rest of their life.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Even though the challenge appears to be great, it is possible and quite simple to overcome.The Member needs to find the courage to face their fears.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Keep on reading on to find out how, as a Member, you can face and overcome your greatest challenge so that you can see for yourself that dreams come true!</p>
                <p><strong>How The Member Archetype Can Master Their Greatest Challenge</strong></p>
                <p>Given the points highlighted above, it&rsquo;s easy to see that The Member needs to accept that they will be rejected and disliked by others for that is part of life.When all is said and done nobody appeals to everybody.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If the Member can begin to integrate this notion that they will be rejected and learn how to handle the inevitable rejection so that they won&rsquo;t allow it to cut deeply in the future, then they can begin to build a sense of self from the inside out, rather from the outside in.Such means that their sense of self will not be conditioned on how everybody perceives them, instead it will be conditioned by how those they are close to perceives them, combined with how they see themselves.</p>
                <p>And if the Member can learn to see themselves as they are, rather than as they have perceived themselves to be because of external feedback, then it becomes easy to build a robust, resilient and balanced sense of identity.Such means that they can find a deep sense of belonging and connection with those who do like, love and accept them for better and for worse - and anybody who doesn&rsquo;t have good intentions toward the Member, or who don&rsquo;t take the time to get to know them won&rsquo;t influence the Members esteem in a negative manner.</p>
                <p>This way, instead of circling downwards as the Member would have been doing before they faced their greatest challenge, they start to spiral upwards as the cycle repeats.This time the Member socializes and uses their talents to network and build relationships, but they take time to show themselves to the people around them and use that as a strategy to filter out those who do not align with them.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This means that eventually, they surround themselves, most of the time, with people who are genuinely invested in them, and who accept them - which continues to improve the Members sense of self and allows the Member to allow their charisma to shine. This improves as they start to feel a deep sense of belonging that they probably never dreamed was possible.As they do this, they continue to realize their dreams by inspiring others, to do the same so that eventually those around the Member also feel as though they belong - and feel free to connect with the Member wholeheartedly.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Which is a perfect situation for the everybody involved!</p>
