            <div class="step7-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?> Archetype - Conclusion</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/joy.png">
                <p>Few archetypes will ever be as popular socially as The Member archetype, however, even though the Member seeks to connect and belong through their social encounters they often don&rsquo;t feel as popular and accepted as they are.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The Member &rsquo;s commitment to listening to others and building rapport with people is outstanding. But because they hold back so much of themselves, the potential for connection is always going to be limited to superficial levels because the Member doesn&rsquo;t share all of themselves.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>And to connect and feel a sense of belonging you need to be able to share yourself so that you can find those people who resonate with you and move on from those who don't.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The problem is that the Member allows all of the people who don&rsquo;t resonate with them to influence their perception of themselves.They fear rejection so much that they haven&rsquo;t usually learned how to discern and accept that they are not going to appeal to everyone and thus, rejection from any man and his dog will all hit a Member to the core.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>So, it&rsquo;s hardly surprising that the Member fears rejection so much.</p>
                <p>As soon as the Member rings the changes suggested above and learns to keep on moving on when it comes to &lsquo;haters&rsquo; then they will find that it&rsquo;s much easier for them to reveal themselves and build deep connections with others.Just not everyone!</p>
                <p>And when the Member learns how to do this, then they really will achieve a deep sense of belonging and their esteem and sense of self will increase tenfold.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>However, for most Members, they might not notice that they even have a problem (despite the lack of deep connections they experience). They may not realize that they are even overlooking or distracting themselves from what they need to do to feel fulfilled and connected which means that many Members are at risk of only achieving low-level relationships and of losing their sense of self quickly if they do reveal themselves.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It doesn&rsquo;t have to be that way though, it is easy for the Member to make the adjustments they need, and the reward is far greater than they would imagine, all they need to do is some inner work, and here at Individualogist.com, we have all of the tools you need to get you started.</p>
                <p>What you have read so far is just an introduction and a tiny portion of what we can tell you about The Member Archetype. It doesn&rsquo;t matter where you are as a Member in your journey; whether you&rsquo;ve already heard your &lsquo;call to action&rsquo; and may have started to implement the changes you must make to overcome your greatest challenge.Whether you&rsquo;ve already achieved a sense of &lsquo;contribution.&rsquo;Or whether you have found this report to be eye-opening from the offset.</p>
                <p>The thing is, we &lsquo;get you,&rsquo; we know your call to action or your greatest challenge, we know the lessons you have to learn and how you might respond to them, and if you felt as though we understood you, that was because we do.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>We know how to help you to uncover and reconcile the hidden aspects of your &lsquo;self&rsquo; so that when you do, all internal conflict fades away and what is left behind is a balanced, whole and strong individual who can navigate life on their terms while connecting with the right people deeply.</p>
                <p>We have spent years understanding the Member Archetype and have built on and adapted Jung&rsquo;s work to ensure that you achieve great success in your quest for liberation.</p>
                <p>We continue to learn more about you and update our content as you send in your life stories and experiences.</p>
                <p>Slowly and surely, we have understood how the Member thinks, relates and connects.Why they do what they do and what they need to discover to reach their full potential.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This is how we know that many of the challenges you&rsquo;ve faced and will face in the future have been and can be reconciled, even if you cannot see how at this moment in time.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>But to reconcile your &lsquo;self,&rsquo; YOU need to understand more about yourself. You need to discover your little (and big) traits so that you can understand them, accept them and work with them, or change them (if they do not serve you).&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Life is fleeting, and you don&rsquo;t have to live your life in conflict and disruption because of your disdain for freedom. You don&rsquo;t have to stand by, and watch others make the changes to the world that you are so capable of doing.You can make changes in the world, and you can learn to bring about change without feeling trapped by limitation. You just need to learn how.</p>
                <p>To learn how, you need to go much deeper into your psyche, and start to uncover the secrets that you keep even from yourself, you need to learn about the secret lives of your unexpressed world and understand how your underworld can cause conflict in your reality - and then you need to learn how to reconcile it.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Once you&rsquo;ve learned about your hidden self, you need to protect your newly found sense of wholeness.You can do this by learning how hidden forces influenced by timing, affect different phases of your life, forces that are seeking to achieve wholeness and are prompting you to reconcile parts of yourself so that you can feel complete; this is all part of the process of individuation.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Most people don&rsquo;t realize that these forces exist and then when they walk into problems in later life they are completely mystified as to how the new challenges they face came about!&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If you can develop an awareness of these factors and build strategies into your life by reconciling them as part of the individuation process, you will be able to conquer your shadows before them conquering you.&nbsp;</p>
